+# Japanese (ja) glossary for the RTX Remix menus
+
+## Style
+
+- Labels, buttons, headers and combo entries: short noun phrases (体言止め).
+  - "Enable X" (checkbox or button) -> 「X を有効化」; "Disable X" -> 「X を無効化」
+  - "Show X" -> 「X を表示」; "Use X" -> 「X を使用」; "X Mode" -> 「X モード」
+  - States: Enabled -> 有効, Disabled -> 無効, On -> オン, Off -> オフ
+- Tooltips, descriptions and messages: です/ます調, full sentences, 、 and 。
+  - "Enables X" -> 「X を有効にします。」; "Whether X" -> 「X するかどうか」
+- A half-width space between Japanese text and an adjacent Latin word, identifier or number
+  (「DLSS を有効化」, 「最大 8 個」), but not next to Japanese punctuation 、。「」.
+- Punctuation that mirrors the English structure stays half-width: `( )`, `:`, `...`, `->`, `[ ]`,
+  `/`, `%`, `~`, `<=`, `>=`. No full-width spaces, no full-width letters or digits.
+- English double quotes around a UI name or term -> 「」; quotes around a literal value, file name or
+  code stay `"..."` (or backticks if the English uses them).
+- Kept in English: option names (`rtx.*`, `dxvk.*`), file names, env vars, backticked text, key
+  names (Alt+X, Ctrl, Shift), numbers and units, and the product or technique names in the brief
+  (RTX, Remix, DLSS, DLSS-RR, DLSS-FG, DLAA, NRD, ReBLUR, ReLAX, ReSTIR GI, RTXDI, NRC, SHaRC, NEE,
+  XeSS, FSR, TAA-U, NIS, Reflex, USD, HDR, ACES, AgX, OMM, PSR, PSTR, GI, IBL, SSS, LOD, BLAS, TLAS,
+  VRAM, GPU, CPU, Vulkan, D3D9, ImGui, Numos, Garry's Mod (GMod), Nsight, RTX Remix Toolkit).
+- Identifiers shown as values (`D3DFOG_EXP`, `AutoExposure_Histogram`, enum names) stay as they are.
