+# zh-CN glossary (Simplified Chinese, mainland conventions)
+
+Terms follow NVIDIA's Chinese UI (GeForce/NVIDIA App, NVIDIA China site) where one exists.
+
+## Style
+
+- Labels, buttons, combo entries: short noun or verb phrases, no full stop.
+- Tooltips and descriptions: full sentences ending in 。, full-width punctuation ，。：；（）“”.
+- A half-width space between Chinese and Latin words or numbers (启用 DLSS, 每像素 1 次采样); none
+  next to full-width punctuation.
+- Parentheses: （） around Chinese text, () around Latin text, units or numbers, e.g. 延迟 (ms).
+- A trailing colon after Chinese text becomes ：; trailing spaces and `...` are kept exactly as in
+  the English.
+- UI names quoted in sentences use “”; quotes that are part of a value, path or code stay ASCII.
+- Kept as written: `rtx.*`/`dxvk.*` options, file names, environment variables, anything in
+  backticks, keys (Alt+X, Ctrl, Shift), numbers and units (ms, px, MB, GB, fps, %, m, K, EV, nits),
+  product and technique names (RTX, Remix, NVIDIA, DLSS, DLSS-RR, DLSS-FG, DLAA, NRD, ReBLUR, ReLAX,
+  ReSTIR, ReSTIR GI, RTXDI, NRC, SHaRC, NEE, XeSS, FSR, TAA, TAA-U, NIS, Reflex, USD, HDR, SDR, ACES,
+  AgX, OMM, PSR, PSTR, GI, IBL, SSS, LOD, BLAS, TLAS, VRAM, GPU, CPU, Vulkan, D3D9, Garry's Mod,
+  ImGui, Numos), and short code words that name a mode or value.
+- printf conversions unchanged and in order; a literal percent sign in a format string is `%%`.
