+# zh-TW glossary (Traditional Chinese, Taiwan)
+
+Taiwan terms throughout (not mainland ones): 檔案, 記憶體, 效能, 品質, 支援, 資訊, 顯示卡, 程式, 資料,
+物件, 預設值, 自訂, 進階, 介面, 視窗, 選單, 螢幕, 網路, 硬體, 軟體, 驅動程式, 快取, 雜湊.
+
+## Style
+
+- Labels, buttons, combo entries: short noun or verb phrases, no sentence-final 。.
+- Tooltips and descriptions: full sentences ending in 。; full-width punctuation in Chinese text
+  (，。：；！？、「」（）).
+- Parentheses: full-width （） when the content has Chinese, half-width ( ) when it is only Latin
+  letters, numbers or units, e.g. `(ms)`, `(DLSS)`.
+- A trailing colon of a label becomes the full-width colon `：` after Chinese text and stays `:` after
+  Latin text or numbers. A trailing `...` stays `...`.
+- Quoted UI names and values use 「」; text in backticks and option names stay exactly as written.
+- One half-width space between Chinese and Latin words or numbers: 啟用 DLSS、2 次反彈、10 ms.
+- No emoji, arrows or math symbols the English does not use; write `->`, `<=`, `>=`, `~`.
+
+## Kept in English
+
+Option and file names (`rtx.*`, `dxvk.*`, `rtx.conf`, `user.conf`, `mod.usda`, `*.dll`), env
+variables, key names (Alt+X, Ctrl, Shift), numbers and units (ms, px, MB, GB, fps, %, m, cm, km, K,
+EV, nits), product and technique names: RTX, Remix, NVIDIA, DLSS, DLSS-RR, DLSS-FG, DLAA, NRD,
+ReBLUR, ReLAX, ReSTIR, ReSTIR GI, RTXDI, NRC, SHaRC, NEE, XeSS, FSR, TAA, TAA-U, NIS, Reflex, USD,
+HDR, SDR, ACES, AgX, OMM, PSR, PSTR, GI, IBL, SSS, LOD, BLAS, TLAS, VRAM, GPU, CPU, Vulkan, D3D9,
+Garry's Mod, ImGui, Numos, Bridge, mip, froxel, prim, spp, EV100, LUT, AABB, UI, alpha, G-buffer.
